-- chair-step: ten UPDATEs on our own door register (platform.client_callable_door.argument_rules).
--   NON-ADDITIVE BY CONSTRUCTION. Nothing is created, dropped or granted, no function body is
--   touched, and no row of anybody's data is read, written or moved. Inverse:
--   migrations/inverse/argsruled2_every_argument_of_the_last_ten_doors_says_what_it_is_down.sql,
--   which restores each row's argument_rules to exactly what it held (seven NULL; the three
--   portal/import rows their 2026-09 declarations).
-- lock: platform
-- lane: ARGS-RULED-2
--
-- ARGS-RULED-2 — THE PER-ARGUMENT CENSUS'S LAST TEN DOORS, RULED FROM THEIR OWN BODIES AND
-- FROM A MEASURED ANSWER, NEVER FROM A PATTERN (lesson 28: a false declaration is worse than
-- none).
--
-- `platform.definer_two_id_population()` named ten client-callable SECURITY DEFINER doors with
-- nineteen id arguments whose door row says nothing about what a FOREIGN id gets. Every rule
-- below was read from the live body and then MEASURED from test@test.com's `authenticated`
-- seat on the MAIN database (a member, not a platform admin — the platform-admin arm hides
-- one of these holes) in a rolled-back world of two organizations: Willow Creek Veterinary
-- Clinic, the caller's own, and High Desert Equine Services, a tenant she is not in.
--
-- Three of the ten were REAL HOLES and were closed FIRST, so what is declared here is what is
-- true after them, never before:
--   public.cat_write           argsruled2_a_stranger_cannot_learn_a_category_exists.sql
--   custom.hub_changed_by      argsruled2_the_hub_describes_only_what_you_may_open.sql
--   public.fork_shared_*(3)    argsruled2_a_private_id_answers_as_an_invented_one.sql
--
-- Two earlier declarations were FALSE and are corrected: portal_archive and portal_restore
-- promised 42501 for a NULL organization; the body answers 22004 (measured). And the import
-- door's NULL Table was declared 23503; it answers in-band, refusing every column by name.
--
-- Every argument is ruled, not only the ids, because the generated door contract
-- (aidream/db/generate_door_contract_test.py) calls a door POSITIONALLY over the arguments its
-- rules name — a rule set that named three of cat_write's eighteen would be uncallable.
--
-- Seat proof: scripts/campaign-tests/argsruled2_holes_green.sql, argsruled2_fork_green.sql.

set lock_timeout = '4s';

